From b4fc052d0a2a13628e2026958449bcd7f578c607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gary Ng <garyng.zhongbo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Send C-BSpace as ^H to a program without extended keys

A terminal in kitty or modifyOtherKeys mode sends Ctrl+Backspace as
its own key (CSI 127;5u), which tmux reads as C-BSpace. A program that
has not asked for extended keys gets keys in the standard form, and
input_key_vt10x has none for Ctrl with DEL, so it dropped the key: in
a popup, where no key binding can turn it into something else,
Ctrl+Backspace did nothing. Send ^H, as xterm and Windows Terminal do
for Ctrl+Backspace outside those modes.
---
 input-keys.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/input-keys.c b/input-keys.c
index fdce540..3171b7b 100644
--- a/input-keys.c
+++ b/input-keys.c
@@ -529,6 +529,8 @@ input_key_vt10x(struct bufferevent *bev, key_code key)
 			key = onlykey - '\030';
 		else if (onlykey >= '@' && onlykey <= '~')
 			key = onlykey & 0x1f;
+		else if (onlykey == 0x7f)
+			key = C0_BS;	/* C-BSpace, as terminals send it */
 		else
 			return (-1);
 	}
